  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Solid sphere <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is rotating about an axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>. If the radius of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, then its radius of gyration about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d9f8350c-05eb-4236-831b-9000e0873bcc-9893891.PNG\" style=\"width: 283px; height: 260px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "110",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d9f8350c-05eb-4236-831b-9000e0873bcc-9893891.PNG\" style=\"width: 283px; height: 260px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Using parallel axis theorem,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>COM&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>[</mo><mn>110</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>110</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>110</mn></math>.</p>",
